The paper’s decisive route is Lemma 3.3: for any graph \(G\), its 1-subdivision \(H\) is bipartite, every PCF \(k\)-coloring of \(H\) restricts to a proper \(k\)-coloring of \(G\), and for \(k\ge5\) every proper coloring of \(G\) can be extended greedily. That gives a construction-backed certificate without solving the generated instance. The viable candidate is therefore a paper-licensed PCF-coloring family, with the answer represented compactly by its colors on the original vertices and checked by executing the lemma’s extension.
